WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.310
(upbeat music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.850
- All right, we are almost out of time.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.630
Give it up for my band, y'all, real quick!

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.059
(audience cheering)
Yay!

00:00:09.059 --> 00:00:10.380
We are almost out of time,

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.540
but there's just enough
for one more great story.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.743
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:13.743 --> 00:00:16.470
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.110
Check out this adorable stuffed elephant.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.480
Come on, her name is Baby Chaba,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.870
and she's named after a
real-life elephant in Thailand.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.210
The real Baby Chaba was rescued from abuse

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.280
thanks to the efforts of many activists,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.070
including a California
mama who created this doll.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.690
And proceeds from this plushie

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.570
are helping rescue even more
elephants, which is so cool.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.100
Let's get this super mama in here.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.210
Say hi to Kristina,

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.420
watching on KSBY in the
lovely Santa Barbara.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.248
What's up, Kristina?
(audience cheering)

00:00:44.248 --> 00:00:46.888
- Hi, Kelly, thanks so much for having me.

00:00:46.888 --> 00:00:50.910
- Hi, so how long have
you been doing this work?

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.280
- So I started over 20 years ago.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.040
I actually saw a baby
elephant being abused

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.300
in the streets of Thailand,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.820
and this was before social
media or anything like that.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.557
So I was distraught by it and I was like,

00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:06.180
"I can't not unsee this," once
you see something like that.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.650
So I came back from Santa Barbara

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.920
and I started protesting
circuses and signing petitions,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.110
but it just didn't feel like enough.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.020
And I think when you have a
calling so strongly like this,

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.550
you have to do something.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:20.430
And so I saw my daughters one day

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.140
playing with stuffed animals

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.850
and I decided to use my background

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.830
in product development and design

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:26.940
and create a stuffed animal

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.370
to help raise funds
and awareness for them.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.160
So that was kind of my goal.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.360
I knew that the girls

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.780
were kind of the most
affected by the abuse,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.840
and I really wanted to
teach children everywhere

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.430
that one person can make a difference

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.740
and that we all need to be
the voice for the voiceless.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.780
- Absolutely, and when you see something,

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.460
you can be part of the
change to make that happen.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.360
I love that.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.550
So this is also about educating everybody,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.380
but including kids, right?

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.880
- Yeah, definitely.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.090
I think it's so important to
teach the younger generation.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.220
And so, you know, it started

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.380
just as a philanthropic toy company,

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.990
but I've started to
teach children in Africa

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.410
about how it's so important to
be friendly to the elephants

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.243
and nice to them,

00:02:08.243 --> 00:02:11.070
and why it's important
for their environment.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.350
And it's so important to teach them

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:17.520
that elephants are really
emotional creatures.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.530
That's the book I wrote for Lek Chailert

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.470
with my friend Pedro de la
Cruz here in Santa Barbara.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.630
But I wanted people everywhere to know

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.090
that we shouldn't ride
them or exploit elephants,

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.370
and I thought I'd start with the children.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.180
And I'm super grateful for the
momentum and all the support.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.340
- Oh man, this is incredible
work you're doing.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.290
And so important, because a
lot of times we do see things

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.340
and we don't know what to do.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.620
So it's important to know
that you can actually

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.970
be a part of like positive change.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.410
And I think it's smart
to start with the kids,

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.700
'cause then at a very young age

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.470
they learn a respect for animals,

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.110
and then, you know, maybe
don't become the adults

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.303
that we have around us today sometimes.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.330
So teach them to be better than us.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.100
Thank you so much, Kristina.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.660
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:58.743
I love little Chaba.

00:02:59.953 --> 00:03:01.020
And that's not all,

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.820
our season-long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:03.660
makers of the G2,

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.130
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.740
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, ma'am.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.480
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.518
for $1,000 to use to continue
your incredible work.

00:03:13.518 --> 00:03:14.778
(audience clapping)

00:03:14.778 --> 00:03:16.678
Thank you so much

00:03:16.678 --> 00:03:18.540
for joining us from the
lovely Santa Barbara.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:19.440
That place is so awesome.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.970
But thank you to all our
guests, this hour as well,

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:24.217
Taylor and Taylor Lautner, Alex Astor,

00:03:24.217 --> 00:03:26.310
Asi Wind, Jackie and Jay Brown.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.630
Y'all have a great day.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.700
And if it's not, try and change it.

